<<<
3. With seem, appear, & the like,

people get puzzled over the com-

binations of the present & past of

seem &c. with the present & perfect

of the infinitive. The possible com-

binations are: He seems to know,

He seems to have known, He seemed to know, He seemed to have

known.
===
3. With *seem, appear,* & the like, people get puzzled over the combinations of the present & past of *seem* &c. with the present & perfect of the infinitive. The possible combinations are: He seems to know, He seems to have known, He seemed to know, He seemed to have known.
>>>

